From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Subject: media: cedrus: run the H616 VE at 624 MHz

The vendor library's clock policy for this decoder (IP version 0x33010,
the H616 entry of its policy list) is 624 MHz; the driver used 600 MHz.

4K 10-bit output to P010 is bound by the VE itself: with two requests
in flight the m2m queue keeps the engine busy over 97% of the time, and
the remaining cost per picture is the engine's (the secondary P010 write
next to the AFBC reconstruction). Measured on an Orange Pi Zero2
(VE-only rate, 4K60 test streams):

                        600 MHz   624 MHz
  H.265 Main10 -> P010  61.1 fps  63.3 fps
  AVS2 Main10 -> P010   59.4 fps  61.7 fps
  VP9 Profile 2 -> P010 58.2 fps  59.5 fps

All three stay bit-exact at 624 MHz, also over a 15 minute md5 loop with
the shared VDD-SYS rail at its 900 mV floor (GPU idle).

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus.c
@@ -1114,7 +1114,12 @@
 			  CEDRUS_CAPABILITY_AVS2_DEC |
 			  CEDRUS_CAPABILITY_JPEG_DEC |
 			  CEDRUS_CAPABILITY_AVS_DEC,
-	.mod_rate	= 600000000,
+	/*
+	 * The vendor policy rate for this decoder (libVE, IP 0x33010).
+	 * 4K 10-bit P010 output is bound by the VE: 600 MHz leaves H.265
+	 * Main10 at 61 fps and AVS2 at 59-60, 624 MHz gives 63 and 62.
+	 */
+	.mod_rate	= 624000000,
 	/*
 	 * With the 128-bit DDR mode, H.264 and VP8 read corrupted reference
 	 * chroma (luma is fine); the 256-bit mode decodes all codecs correctly.
